@flexiarg operator/name-the-done-signal-act
@title Name the Act That Signals Done
@status accepted 2026-11-11: proposed by 象 for 22 turns (Joe 2026-11-11: recurrence suffices); attested once used in a mission or a War Machine cascade
@provenance 象 proposals, ~/.emacs-graph/session-turn-analysis/<record>[.json].candidates.json; records: turn-6bjr40 turn-7OqIIk turn-BwJv21 turn-CTt1G8 turn-KtSTA7 turn-MvH0V0 turn-Que9fD turn-VGG5nt turn-aaQK7Z turn-bvXQD8 turn-e04dpT turn-hCreYh turn-hshWUH turn-hyepbx turn-k20X5K turn-kGaFGa turn-lKCBbO turn-lO7uLw turn-nYzx66 turn-rPdt9m turn-tGc77o turn-uL9Sth
@parent apparatus/done-is-observed-running
@context An agent (codex-18) is running a pinned Python-to-LISP port under a standing 'please continue' with no defined end condition.

! conclusion: Attach the completion condition and the exact signalling act to the continue: 'when X is complete, evaluate Y to signal completion and readiness for the next phase'.

  + IF:
    The task has a recognisable completion state and a concrete agent-executable act exists that can serve as the completion signal.

  + HOWEVER:
    Without a named off-switch, the continue-loop has no way to end cleanly or to communicate readiness for the next phase.

  + THEN:
    Attach the completion condition and the exact signalling act to the continue: 'when X is complete, evaluate Y to signal completion and readiness for the next phase'.

  + BECAUSE:
    It is the operator-side prescription of that pattern's observable done-state: the operator pre-names the act whose performance constitutes done.
